  "$mirrors_comment": "Units we have COMMITTED to keeping in step. The existence check FAILS when one is missing from a language that is required to have it. This is the half a conformance corpus cannot do: a fixture table compares two implementations and reports that they disagree, but it can never fail on ABSENCE, because a missing mirror has nothing to run the rows against. Drift and existence are different mechanisms and this repository ships both.",
  "mirrors": [
    {
      "unit": "capability:text",
      "kind": "capabilities",
      "required_in": [
        "php",
        "ts",
        "py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "unit": "provider:openai",
      "kind": "providers",
      "required_in": [
        "php",
        "ts",
        "py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "unit": "feature:value-object-serialization",
      "kind": "features",
      "required_in": [
        "php",
        "ts",
        "py"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "$deferred_comment": "Units present in the reference that the ports deliberately do NOT have yet. Listed so the drift report can tell a decision apart from an oversight — an unlisted absence is drift and gets reported; a listed one is the plan.",
  "deferred": [
    {
      "unit": "feature:tool-execution-loop",
      "reason": "Out of the vertical slice. Tools can be declared and tool calls parsed, but the multi-step execution loop, approvals and concurrency are a much larger surface and porting them before the mapping patterns settled would have replicated whatever is wrong with them."
    },
    {
      "unit": "feature:tool-approval",
      "reason": "Deferred WITH the execution loop, and listed separately only because it was an oversight not to be. Approving a tool call is a decision made mid-loop; a port that can parse a tool call and not run one has nothing to approve. It becomes portable when the loop does, and is not a separate piece of work."
    },
    {
      "unit": "feature:value-object-rehydration",
      "reason": "Present in the PORTS and absent from the reference, which is the unusual direction. particle-academy/prism can serialise its value objects and cannot read them back; see finding F-4."
    },
    {
      "unit": "feature:telemetry",
      "reason": "Deliberately deferred. Telemetry is Laravel-event-shaped in the reference and a port should not inherit that shape without a decision about what the equivalent is."
    },
    {
      "unit": "feature:threads",
      "reason": "Deferred with telemetry: the Thread contract is one method, but its value is in the Eloquent/storage integrations around it."
    }
  ],
